Gloves of dexterity only improve your dexterity if they are
enchanted.  If I find gloves of dexterity early, I'll certainly
choose them over leather, and if I find them enchanted, so much
the better---they really will make a difference.  By the time
I've got the scrolls (identified) to enchant them, however, I've
usually got luck max'ed out, and enough XP so that my chance to
hit is 100%, with or without them.  So I'll definitely not waste
a wish on them (unless, maybe, I found two fully charged wands
of wishing in the early levels, in which case, +2 dexterity is
probably better than just never using the wish).

